<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!-- SHIP_VERMIN_MOD_1. insertTag="Animal_PreMain" is vanilla's own extension
     point (Verse.AI.ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag, RimSage-verified: every
     ThinkTreeDef sharing an insertTag is tried, in insertPriority order, for
     EVERY animal in the game whose think tree includes that tag - the
     vanilla "Animal" tree does, unconditionally). Both JobGivers below
     return no job instantly for any pawn whose race lacks their matching
     DefModExtension (RM_SeekTargetExtension / RM_GnawTargetExtension), so
     this is safe to insert globally: an un-tagged chicken or muffalo never
     sees a behavior change.

     DESERT_SHADE_WHALE_FILTERFEED_1 added RM_JobGiver_FilterFeedTerrain here
     rather than to RM_ThinkTree_ShadeSeekingWander (insertTag
     Animal_PreWander): feeding has to outrank wandering, and it has to be
     tried BEFORE vanilla's own hunger handling so an animal standing on its
     own food does not walk off to find a plant. It sits last in this list on
     purpose - a vermin already mid-gnaw or mid-forage keeps that job, and
     filter-feeding is only reached when nothing more specific wanted the
     tick. It gates on the food need first, so an un-hungry carrier costs one
     float compare. -->
<Defs>

  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>RM_ThinkTree_VerminBehaviors</defName>
    <insertTag>Animal_PreMain</insertTag>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_JobGiver_GnawTargets" />
        <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_JobGiver_SeekMarkedTerrain" />
        <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_JobGiver_SeekShade" />
        <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_ThinkNode_EatCleanable" />
        <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_JobGiver_FilterFeedTerrain" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
